##		- 20141003 JC: Consolidated multiple commands from different scripts, into this one script - so it works more like "git".
##		- 20141104 JC: Finished; added helper commands such as mtm; shortened function names.
##		- 20141110 JC: Fixed a 'merge' bug; function names match arguments; -m for merge or push message; turned off git's editor merge message.
##		- 20141209 JC: Sanitize input message strings of solitary single quotes or double quotes.
##		- 20220501 JC:
##			- Removed 'init', 'setrepo', and 'pushmtm' commands.
##			- Removed the system-wide 'top-level git directory' and '.gitsby_current' concepts; change projects just by changing directories.
##			- Added commands: scommit and scompul.
##			- Changed all 'git pull' to 'git pull --ff-only'.
##		- 20220502 JC: Updated.
##		- 20260722 JC:
##			- Rewrote on the current template generation: strict mode, arg parser, trap suite, minified header trio.
##			- Every command now verifies repo state first and is idempotent: stash only if dirty (and pop only what was pushed), pull only with an upstream, push only if ahead, commit only if there are changes.
##			- Detect main vs master from origin's HEAD instead of a hardcoded name.
##			- Run git via argument arrays instead of eval; dropped the curly-quote message mangling (no longer needed).
##			- mtm merges --no-ff and deletes the merged branch local + remote; guards against running from the default branch.
##			- mkbranch/chbranch validate branch existence up front and park current work (commit+pull+push) before switching.
##			- Added -q/--quiet and -m/--message/--msg; message can still be given positionally.
##			- Removed the unused template library (~1400 lines).
##		- 20260722 JC:
##			- Renamed commands: scompul->saveup, spush->sync, scommit->commit, spull->pull, mkbranch->newbr, chbranch->gobr, list->listbr, mtm->land. Old names still work (hidden aliases).
##			- newbr/gobr/land now target dev when the repo has one, else main/master.
##			- Added pr (list / review / accept, via gh) and release (merge dev into main, tag, push; bumps patch when no version given).
##		- 20260723 JC:
##			- Pre-flight display before the confirm prompt: resolved SSH identity (alias -> real host, user, key), commit author, ahead/behind, and the files an incoming pull would change.
##			- Changed files now list one per line, truncated to the terminal and capped, instead of git status's long form.
##		- 20260723 JC:
##			- Renamed saveup->update (saveup stays as a hidden alias).
##			- release now fast-forwards dev to main afterward so dev includes the release merge and tag; skipped (with a warning) if dev moved mid-release.
##			- Output starts with a blank line for breathing room after the shell prompt.
##		- 20260724 JC:
##			- pull now uses --autostash, so a failed pull leaves the working tree intact instead of leaving work in the stash.
##			- land publishes an upstream-less merge target before deleting the remote work branch.
##			- newbr carries dirty work from main/dev to the new branch instead of committing it there; gobr refuses to auto-commit on those branches.
##		- 20260724 JC:
##			- -h/-v only recognized in the command slot, so a message like "add -v flag" no longer short-circuits the run.
##			- Non-tty mutating runs fail closed without -q; a stray extra word after a message is rejected instead of dropped.
##			- git failures report as a plain one-liner (the trap dump stays for real script errors); printf instead of echo -e so escape bytes in filenames/messages stay inert.
##			- Fetch now prunes, heals origin/HEAD, and gets an ssh connect timeout; --no-fetch skips it entirely.
##			- Displayed remote URLs mask embedded credentials; ssh -G gets --; command -v instead of which; release tolerates short tags like v1.2.
##			- land's remote-branch delete is non-fatal if the branch is already gone; default branch and merge target resolve once per run.
